;# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. Applied at edge before the SPA loads.
#
# docs.orangerails.com is a custom domain on THIS project's own Cloudflare
# Pages deployment (orangerails-prod), the same deployment that contains
# src/routes/docs.tsx. orangerails.com is served by a DIFFERENT Cloudflare
# Pages project (orangerails-marketing), which has no /docs route. A
# visitor on docs.orangerails.com must be kept on this project and pointed
# at its own /docs route, not sent to the marketing project.

# Probe rule: if /redir-probe-2026 returns 302 to /docs/quickstart, the
# parser is reading this file. If it returns 200 (SPA fallback), the file
# is not being parsed at all and the docs.* rule below would never fire
# either.
/redir-probe-2026 /docs/quickstart 302

# docs.orangerails.com shares this deployment, so rewrite (not redirect)
# onto our own /docs route. Status 200 keeps the visitor's URL on
# docs.orangerails.com while serving the docs content from this project.
https://docs.orangerails.com/* /docs/:splat 200

# docs.orangerails.dev is not attached to any Cloudflare Pages project in
# this account. There used to be a rule here pointing it at the marketing
# project; removed rather than left as a rule that looks load bearing but
# can never fire.

# SPA deep-link fallback. MUST be the last rule so the specific rules
# above match first. Cloudflare Pages serves any real static asset
# (JS/CSS/images, index.html) before consulting _redirects, so this only
# fires for paths with no physical file: client-router routes like /docs,
# /docs/xpub-export, /app, /login. The 200 (rewrite, not redirect) serves
# index.html at the requested URL and lets the in-app router take over.
# Without this, those routes 404 on direct load / hard refresh even
# though their source is deployed.
/* /index.html 200
